<title>USA: Invacare seeks Healthdyne annual meeting.</title>
<headline>Invacare seeks Healthdyne annual meeting.</headline>
<dateline>ELYRIA, Ohio 1997-04-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Invacare Corp, which has launched a $173 million hostile takeover of Healthdyne Technologies Inc, said Tuesday it is seeking a court order to try to force Healthdyne to hold its annual shareholders meeting by June 30.</p>
<p>Invacare is seeking to replace Healthdyne's board of directors at the meeting.  </p>
<p>&quot;Healthdyne's failure to schedule its annual meeting is yet another attempt to prevent its shareholders from exercising their rights to elect directors of their own choosing,&quot; Invacare chief executive officer Malachi Mixon said in a news release.</p>
<p>Healthdyne officials were not immediately available for comment.</p>
<p>Shares of Invacare fell 1/16 to 22-15/16 in morning trade. Healthdyne stock declined 1/4 to 14-3/8.</p>
<p>((--Robin Sidel, 212/859-1723))</p>
